@startuml fig8-delete-group
!include style.iuml
title Figure 8 (new): Delete a group with all of its expenses and settlements (FR 1.7; A4, D6)

actor Owner
participant ":GroupDetailActivity" as UI
participant ":ConfirmDialog" as CD
participant ":GroupViewModel" as VM
participant ":GroupRepository" as GR
participant "db : FirebaseFirestore\n(+ security rules)" as DB

Owner -> UI : menu → Delete group\n(only visible to the owner)
UI -> CD : show()
alt Owner taps Cancel
  CD --> UI : nothing happens
else Owner confirms
  CD -> VM : deleteGroup()
  VM -> VM : isOwner()? (re-checked before the write)
  VM -> GR : deleteGroup(groupId, cb)
  GR -> DB : get groups/{groupId}/transactions
  DB --> GR : documents
  GR -> GR : refs = every transaction, then groups/{groupId} last
  loop batches of at most 450 writes, committed one after another
    GR -> DB : WriteBatch.delete(ref) for each ref in the batch; commit()\n(the last batch also deletes groups/{groupId})
    note right of DB
      CHANGED rules: besides each transaction's creator,
      the group owner may delete transactions, otherwise
      a group holding other members' expenses could
      never be deleted (FR 1.7 vs FR 2.7). The owner check
      reads groups/{groupId}, so that document goes last.
    end note
    DB --> GR : ok
  end
  GR --> VM : cb.onSuccess(null)
  VM --> UI : groupDeleted (Event)
  UI --> Owner : "Group deleted", back to the group list
end

legend bottom left
New interaction (not in Project 2.2).
endlegend
@enduml
